good evening police say they found an  explosive device not far from the las  vegas strip  thanks for joining us at six i'm denise  valdez and i'm bryan loftis it is a  story the i-team first broke earlier  today the i-team's vanessa murphy has  more now from  paradise and flamingo you can see how  busy the intersection here at flamingo  and paradise is  this is also just minutes from the las  vegas strip  and it's this area where metro police  say they found  christopher camacho driving around with  a homemade  explosive device in his car according to  this arrest report an  officer stopped camacho after he noticed  an excessive amount of smoke  coming from the exhaust on his honda  civic camacho  told the officer he was recently  released from prison  and there was a bb gun and fireworks in  his car  and he gave officers permission to  search it police say they found a black  pneumatic firearm and the homemade  explosive device  in the back seat the area was blocked  off and the bomb squad and  counterterrorism detectives were called  police determined a copper cylinder had  similar characteristics  to a manufactured explosive device and  powder in a clear tube was similar to  what's in commercial fireworks  investigators say they also found  equipment used for credit card fraud  they searched camacho's motel room on  boulder highway  according to the arrest report they  found equipment used for identity theft  and  credit card fraud in an interview police  say camacho told them he didn't intend  to hurt anyone  and he was going to light off what he  called a firework  in the desert with his son court records  show he faces two felony charges in  connection with the alleged explosive  device  and 11 counts in connection with  financial crimes  the nevada department of corrections  website reveals more about his  history it lists previous convictions  for a drug  charge stealing a car and having a gun  as a felon  camacho's next court date is set for  thursday  vanessa murphy 8 news now
 

